{"id":27816,"slug":"les-cousins","title":"Les cousins","year":1959,"country":"France","duration":109,"spine":581,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/27816-les-cousins","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/56ba3e5cf5c30c4ca37d11dbc92db30c/TIrcSypBNof95PXcIsPiciN0HD59y4_large.jpg","description":"In Les cousins, Claude Chabrol crafts a sly moral fable about a provincial boy who comes to live with his sophisticated bohemian cousin in Paris. Through these seeming opposites, Chabrol conjures a darkly comic character study that questions notions of good and evil, love and jealousy, and success in the modern world. A mirror image of Le beau Serge, Chabrol’s debut, Les cousins recasts that film’s stars, Jean-Claude Brialy and Gérard Blain, in startlingly reversed roles. This dagger-sharp drama won the Golden Bear at the Berlin Film Festival and was an important early entry in the French New Wave.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Claude Chabrol","slug":"claude-chabrol"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Gérard Blain","role":"Charles","slug":"gerard-blain"},{"actor":"Jean-Claude Brialy","role":"Paul","slug":"jean-claude-brialy"},{"actor":"Juliette Mayniel","role":"Florence","slug":"juliette-mayniel"},{"actor":"Guy Decomble","role":"Bookseller","slug":"guy-decomble"},{"actor":"Geneviève Cluny","role":"Geneviève","slug":"genevieve-cluny"},{"actor":"Michèle Méritz","role":"Yvonne","slug":"michele-meritz"},{"actor":"Corrado Guarducci","role":"Count Arcangelo Minerva","slug":"corrado-guarducci"},{"actor":"Stéphane Audran","role":"Françoise","slug":"stephane-audran"},{"actor":"Paul Bisciglia","role":"Marc","slug":"paul-bisciglia"},{"actor":"Jeanne Pérez","role":"Concierge","slug":"jeanne-perez"},{"actor":"Françoise Vatel","role":"Martine","slug":"francoise-vatel"},{"actor":"Claude Cerval","role":"Clovis","slug":"claude-cerval"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Claude Chabrol","slug":"claude-chabrol"},{"role":"Producer","person":"Claude Chabrol","slug